<!--Post: 2337--><!--Time: 1103555943-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2337"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brazilian<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brazilian<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 20, 2004 - 7:19 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I read a lot of posts and theories about BTK큦 real name based on the fact that his true initials are actually BTK. Or W, since some people think his name might be William. <BR> <BR>Personally I dont believe on this. What do you guys think about it?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2337-->
<!--Post: 2384--><!--Time: 1103585366-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2384"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 20, 2004 - 3:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t believe it either Brazilian. BTK offered nine different choices of a nickname. The BTK Strangler was first followed by The Wichita Stangler, The Poetic Strangler, The Bondage Strangler, Psycho, The Wichita Hangman, The Wichita Executioner, The Garote Phantom and The Asphixiator. So he easliy could have been called something else by the media and authorities. <BR>It is interesting that he misspelled the word Garrote. Garrote with two r&#39;s refers to strangulation and methods of strangulation while Garote as he spells it with one r refers to a Filippino martial arts stick. You would think if a serial killer were choosing a name he would look up the correct spelling.  <BR>It is of further interest to note that in a drawing he sent to would-be victim Anna Williams he shows what investigators and others who have seen it, what is described as a billy club or police baton being inserted into a body cavity. Could they have interpreted the drawing incorrectly? Could it be a Garote stick?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2384-->
<!--Post: 2391--><!--Time: 1103590069-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2391"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 20, 2004 - 4:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Its highly unlikely the BTK Strangler would use the initials of his name in the sobriquet. BTK refers to the method of murder and the term Strangler refers to the aspect of the crime that provides him with gratification. A sadistic psychopath enjoys taunting the police and public to ensure he maintains control and domination of the situation.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2391-->
<!--Post: 2774--><!--Time: 1104102312-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2774"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 26, 2004 - 3:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->His initial letter said that the letters b,t, &amp;k were a &#34;code&#34; for &#34;me&#34; which I interpret to mean a code either for himself or for his name.  BTK is an anagram for &#34;bind torture kill&#34;, not a code for it. <BR> <BR>Incidently, the initials BTK also describe another serial killer who was well known to the WSU professor PJ.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2774-->
<!--Post: 2777--><!--Time: 1104106442-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2777"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 26, 2004 - 4:14 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t know, perhaps I&#39;m being pedantic, but the moniker always seemed  to be disjointed to me. <BR>The Bind them, Torture them, Kill them, Stranler. <BR>Technically, shouldn&#39;t it be, Bind, torture, strangle, Kill/killer?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2777-->
<!--Post: 2783--><!--Time: 1104117064-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2783"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Juno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Juno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 26, 2004 - 7:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think he meant code as in  <BR>Code Name: Stingray  <BR>-or- <BR>Code Name: Jet Jaguar <BR>-or- <BR>Code name: BTK <BR>It&#39;s an acronym in this case, much like S.N.A.F.U. <BR>It&#39;s not a code for his real name.  <BR> <BR>Although obvious, it&#39;s interesting to note that all of the &#34;codenames&#34; other than &#34;psycho&#34; have to do with asphyxiation. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2783-->
<!--Post: 2788--><!--Time: 1104123388-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2788"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 26, 2004 - 8:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sorry, I said anagram and meant acronym.   <BR> <BR>That said, the letter didn&#39;t say it&#39;s my &#34;code name&#34;, nor did it say it&#39;s an &#34;acronym for my name&#34;.  &#40;No offense, but if one analyzes the letter by guessing at what he meant by what he said, we&#39;ll be guessing forever.&#41;  If, however, we assume that he used language precisely, and that he meant exactly what he said, then we may have a starting point. <BR>His exact language was: &#34;The code words for me will be... Bind them, toture them, kill them, B.T.K.,&#34; &#40;<a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_packages/btk/history/8321038.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_pack ages/btk/history/8321038.htm</a>&#41; <BR> <BR>If anyone knows of some communication where he said his name was BTK please post it.  The letter with wichita strangler etc asked the press to name him.  BTK is not a name and bind them, toture etc. is not a name.  But if I&#39;m correct he NEVER said his name was BTK.   <BR> <BR>I&#39;m curious about the reasoning behind the statement &#34;It&#39;s not a code for his real name&#34;?  Would you mind sharing it?   <BR> <BR>However, if we treat the letters B, T, and K as code for a name instead of a code name, what&#39;s the name?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2788-->
<!--Post: 2794--><!--Time: 1104144033-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2794"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 27, 2004 - 2:40 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I like Pat Brown&#39;s idea about the initials BTK - that they are related to the Marines in Vietnam, and their slogan &#34;Born To Kill&#34;.  Check out her profile at: <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.she-dc.com/pages/BTK.htm" target=_top>http://www.she-dc.com/pages/BTK.htm</a> <BR> <BR>There almost has to be a direct connection to a Marine vet or wannabe, in my opinion.  I think he really wanted the acronym.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2794-->
<!--Post: 2949--><!--Time: 1104313059-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2949"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 1:37 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Pax56 <BR>there certainly could be a direct connection to a Marine.  Can you build a connection from the letters B T &amp; K to the name of a marine who lived in wichita two blocks from a BTK victim, who owns a business machine/copier repair company, is heavily involved in historical rail lines and is on the donor list at WSU?. What about the other two BTK&#39;s named in her analysis, &#34;Build the Kingdom&#34; and &#34;Billy the Kid&#34;.   <BR> <BR>Billy the Kid was a serial killer &#40;he killed eight people&#41; and actually lived in wichita; historical data locates the residence near 21st and Oliver.   <BR> <BR>The phrase BTK was a name the historical press used as an acronym for Billy the Kid.  To quote Juno since his real name was different &#40;Lets say his real name was John Doe,&#41; Billy the Kid would be John Doe&#39;s code name, which would use BTK like a morse code [SOS = Save Our Ship] so [BTK&#40;morse code&#41; = Billy The Kid &#40;Code name&#41;= John Doe. <BR> <BR>What if you could take Billy the Kid&#39;s real name and do everything I suggested you do with Born To Kill: <BR> <BR>&#34; build a connection from the letters B T &amp; K to the name of a person who lived in wichita two blocks from a BTK victim, who owns a business machine/copier repair company, is heavily involved in historical rail lines and is on the donor list at WSU?.&#34; <BR> <BR>I guess the starting point would be to ask what Billy the Kid&#39;s real name was and whether he had any historical connection to oteros?  <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2949-->
<!--Post: 2999--><!--Time: 1104363928-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2999"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Juno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Juno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 3:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I would posit that the use of the word &#34;code&#34; was simply a malapropism on the part of BTK. <BR> <BR>He was referring to something more akin to &#34;key words&#34; &#34;descriptors&#34; &#34;adjectives&#34; &#34;buzz words&#34; &#34;nom de plume&#34; etc.  I didn&#39;t mean to imply above that it was actually a &#34;code.&#34; <BR> <BR>I seriously doubt they have anything to do with his real initials.  This is a guy who wanted press and wasn&#39;t getting it.  So he made up his own nickname, so to speak. <BR> <BR>Ever see the episode of Seinfeld where George wants a nickname?  He  keeps trying to get people to call him something like &#34;T-Bone.&#34;  That&#39;s about the best analogy I can come up with.  The press wasn&#39;t giving him a Kool Killer Kode-Name so he manufactured his own moniker.  <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2999-->
<!--Post: 3009--><!--Time: 1104370533-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3009"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 5:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Perhaps I should tell more of the reason behind my last post on this thread. <BR> <BR>I followed the line of reasoning outlined in the 12/29/04 post, starting several months ago.  I arrived at a name &#40;which I&#39;m not putting out here because I need an independent review.&#41; <BR> <BR>I have verified that a person by this name meets all available criteria.  When WPD went public with &#34;details&#34; so many of them fit that I called WPD, spent an hour with them, and gave them a copy of my research files.   <BR> <BR>I&#39;m seriously asking for a doublecheck on my reasoning and facts.  I think BTK made a mistake in his early correspondence, and tried to cover it up with his request that we pick a name for him. <BR> <BR>I mean no offense to Juno, but it&#39;s the same cop mentality that I see all the time.  Assumptions are not evidence, they are not facts. You don&#39;t use assumptions to exclude evidence, you use them to test evidence.   <BR> <BR>BTK may have used the word &#34;code&#34; incorrectly and it may indeed be a malapropism.  The only problem is that there is absolutely no evidence to support that conclusion. <BR> <BR>We don&#39;t know what he meant in his letters, but we do know what he said.  I don&#39;t mean to ruffle feathers here, but if you assume/posit that this language was a mistake, the analysis stops right there.  If you assume he meant exactly what he said, you have a testable hypothesis. <BR> <BR>How about looking at his first letter and assuming he meant what he said?   <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3009-->
<!--Post: 3036--><!--Time: 1104378247-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3036"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jujuree<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jujuree<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 7:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;I think BTK made a mistake in his early correspondence, and tried to cover it up with his request that we pick a name for him.&#34; <BR> <BR>I have to ask, what mistake are you referring to?  Can you tell without giving more info than you&#39;re prepared to give? <BR> <BR>Also, are you referring to the letter he left at the Wichita Public Library, addressed to the &#34;Secret Witness Program,&#34; claiming the Otero murders?  That was the first letter, wasn&#39;t it?   <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3036-->
<!--Post: 3053--><!--Time: 1104387307-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3053"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 10:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think you made the right call twice - by going to the WPD and by not publishing the name.  Sounds like they gave you a fair hearing &#40;1 hour&#41;, too, which is refreshing to hear. <BR> <BR>Also consider the possibility that your suspect is not BTK, but a person &#42;known&#42; to BTK.  The reason I&#39;m saying this is that I personally don&#39;t buy many of the clues that he has been giving the police in 2004.  For example, the train thing has a lot of joke-on-the-cops potential.  I really think he may have been setting the police up on a lot of his clues.  But the blowback on that is that he may very well prove to be somebody acquainted with - or even well-known to - several people who fit the released profile, if he indeed tailored it to fit real individuals who he thought would draw police interest and resources. <BR> <BR>In any case, the initials B.T.K. may be significant - they could have multiple connections and meanings that BTK liked. <BR> <BR>It could be coincidence that the initials are a function of your suspect&#39;s name, but it might not be.  If you&#39;re comfortable letting somebody look at you&#39;re reasoning, and if Tom is willing to play postmaster and forward your ideas to me, I&#39;d be happy to look at your ideas offline.  I&#39;d rather not put my email on the board, however, since it&#39;s been getting mega-hits.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3053-->
<!--Post: 3165--><!--Time: 1104537132-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3165"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Juno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Juno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 31, 2004 - 3:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->So, I can assume he meant what he said at face value <BR> <BR>&#42;or&#42; <BR> <BR>I can look at his writing and make some assumptions based on his word choice, sentence structure etc.   <BR> <BR>Either way one is making an assumption. <BR> <BR>Shall I assume he reall meant to say &#34;those three dude?&#34; <BR> <BR>Shall I assume there really is a monster? Who apparently is looking over his shoulder as he writes and getting in a few lines of his own? <BR> <BR>Did he really mean &#34;BTK Haunts&#34; as it first appeared  or the later, apparently corrected, &#34;BTK&#39;s Haunts?&#34;  Did he really mean &#34;will there more?&#34; or the again corrected &#34;Will There Be More?&#34; <BR> <BR>Looking at his writing, I would not be surprised if he misuses words.  He has already done so. <BR> <BR>I will assume he uses words incorrectly, wanted attention, and came up with his own media name.  Is that more or less plausible than to assume he was dumb enough to use his real initials....and is still at large? <BR> <BR>Writing style analysis is a very worthwhile tool. <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3165-->
<!--Post: 3225--><!--Time: 1104639696-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3225"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 01, 2005 - 8:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Actually one can analyze it both ways. <BR>   <BR>However, you should be careful to start with the literal language.  He didn&#39;t say they were &#34;his real initials&#34; what he said was: <BR> <BR> <BR>&#34;The code words for me will be... Bind them, toture them, kill them, B.T.K.,&#34; <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR>I will concede that if your assumption is correct, &#34;he uses words incorrectly, wanted attention, and came up with his own media name&#34;, then I&#39;m on a wild goose chase. <BR> <BR>But what if my assumption is correct?   <BR> <BR> <BR>Look at <a href="http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~gazetteer2000/ham_city/cemetery/oakwood/r_oakw/billykid.htm" target=_top>http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~gazetteer 2000/ham_city/cemetery/oakwood/r_oakw/billykid.htm</a> <BR> <BR>Pax56: Set up a pseudonym email with yahoo, and email me at <a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com">whoisbtk@yahoo.com</a>. I will email a detailed summary.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3225-->
<!--Post: 3324--><!--Time: 1104803844-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3324"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 5:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Although I don&#39;t believe BTK stands for anything but Bind, Torture, Kill it could have a double meaning when refering to something he takes with him to all his murder sites.  <BR>That would be his Basic Tool Kit.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3324-->
